Fisica Scale SDK License
Version 2.0 (draft for review, revised 2026-10-17)

This version states the product policy of 2026-10-17 (SDK keys, basic and full mode) and
is published for review. It has not completed legal review. The text first published
under this version number on 2026-10-14 is superseded; doc/policy-history.md records the
change. This version does not change any existing agreement, any package already delivered
under Version 1.0 (doc/LICENSE-1.0.txt), or any rights granted under an earlier license
such as the MIT License.

Copyright (c) 2026 Care&Co. All rights reserved.

1. Scope and definitions

This license applies to the Fisica Scale SDK materials distributed by Care&Co under it:
public language wrappers, examples, documentation, public C headers and the compiled
native core.

- "Hardware" means a genuine Fisica Scale lawfully obtained from Care&Co or an
  authorized channel.
- "Public Wrappers" means wrapper source expressly provided by Care&Co.
- "Native Core" means the compiled implementation and its private source.
- "Developer Portal" means https://developer.fisicahealthcare.com, where Care&Co
  publishes SDK documentation and the current conditions referred to in this license.
- "Basic Mode" and "Full Mode" are the two ways the SDK operates (sections 2 and 3).
- "Trial", "Extension" and "Contract" are the three ways to obtain Full Mode
  (section 3); together, a "Grant".
- "SDK Key" means a key signed by Care&Co for one Grant, issued in the Developer Portal.
  Each SDK Key is one seat.
- "Target" means what an SDK Key is activated for: one application, identified by its
  application ID (bundle ID or package name; its debug builds are the same application),
  or one computer, identified by a hash of its machine identifier.
- "Separate Agreement" means a written agreement with Care&Co for the matters in
  section 6, which may be part of a Contract.

2. Base SDK License: Basic Mode (included with the Hardware)

Purchase of the Hardware includes a non-exclusive license to use the SDK with that
Hardware in Basic Mode, for any purpose, including commercial applications, services and
facility measurements and charging your own customers for them. The Base SDK License has
no date-based expiry and needs no SDK Key, registration or signed agreement.

Basic Mode provides connection, measurement, device settings and calibration, weight,
foot length and width, a real-time preview at a limited frame rate, and report
summaries. Care&Co does not disable Basic Mode on the basis of registration, SDK Key,
Grant or contract status.

3. Full Mode

Full Mode adds the features described in the Developer Portal, such as raw packets and
raw or processed sensor grids, full-rate frames, full report exports and future advanced
analysis. It is available only while an SDK Key of a valid Grant is activated for the
Target that uses it, within the key's validity and the Grant's full-mode period.

- Trial: available once per account, organization, business registration number and
  Target, after Care&Co approves the request. Its length, seats and features are those
  approved and shown in the Developer Portal.
- Extension: free Full Mode for non-commercial education, research or public and
  non-profit use, granted at Care&Co's discretion for the period, seats and features it
  approves.
- Contract: commercial use of Full Mode after a Trial requires a Contract. Its period,
  seats, features, monthly seat moves, longest key validity, any grace period after its
  end and any rights under section 6 are those stated in the Contract and the Developer
  Portal.

When a Grant, a key's validity or a grace period ends, or a key is released or
revoked, the SDK continues in Basic Mode. Ending Full Mode does not end the Base SDK
License, ownership of the Hardware or the registration of devices, and end users of
lawfully supplied applications keep Basic Mode.

4. SDK Keys and seats

- Each SDK Key is one seat. A Grant has the number of seats Care&Co approved or agreed,
  and an SDK Key may be created only within them.
- An SDK Key is activated once for one Target and gives Full Mode only on that Target.
  An application Target covers every installation of that application; a computer
  Target covers that computer only.
- Releasing a key frees its seat when the device lets go of the key, a release code from
  the device is entered in the Developer Portal, the key's validity ends, or Care&Co
  releases it. Creating a key in a released seat is a seat move; seat moves are limited
  per month as stated for the Grant.
- An application ID may be used under one Contract or Grant at a time. You may not
  resell, transfer or share an SDK Key, a Target or a Grant, or use an SDK Key for an
  application or computer it was not activated for, except as a Separate Agreement
  allows.
- Keep SDK Keys within your organization and the products that use them. Care&Co may
  revoke an SDK Key that is used against this license.

5. Registration and requests

A Trial, Extension or Contract is requested in the Developer Portal with the account,
organization and project details it asks for; commercial requests include the
applicant's contact details. Care&Co reviews each request and may approve, adjust or
decline it. Registration details are used for these requests, support and administering
this license. They are not a unit of runtime tracking.

6. Matters that need a Separate Agreement

The Base SDK License and a Grant do not include, and a Separate Agreement is required
for:

- selling or distributing the SDK on its own, or reselling the SDK;
- OEM integration and supply of the Hardware or SDK under another party's product;
- rebranding the Hardware;
- use of the SDK with anything other than the Hardware;
- any other exception to these terms.

Paid support, cloud or analysis services are offered, if at all, under their own
agreements.

7. Public Wrappers: modification and redistribution

Within these terms you may use, copy and modify the Public Wrappers and include them,
together with the unmodified compiled Native Core, in your own applications and
products for distribution to your users. Keep this license and the applicable copyright
and third-party notices, and identify your modifications so they are not presented as
an unmodified Care&Co release. Your users' rights must be consistent with this license.
You may not sublicense the SDK on terms that remove these conditions.

8. Native Core, reverse engineering and retained rights

No Native Core source is provided or licensed for disclosure, modification or
redistribution. Do not distribute private implementation source, debug symbols or
internal build materials. You may not decompile, disassemble or otherwise reverse
engineer the Native Core, or modify, bypass or disable how the SDK decides between Basic
Mode and Full Mode, except to the extent applicable law expressly permits it despite
this restriction, for example for interoperability. Rights not expressly granted are
reserved. Nothing here restricts rights that cannot lawfully be restricted.

9. Licensing operation and data

The Native Core reads the Target itself and decides the mode from the signed SDK Key.
Online, the SDK activates a new SDK Key and renews it before it expires; a computer that
is never online uses an activation code and key files from the Developer Portal.

- Activation sends the SDK Key and the Target (the application ID, or the hash of the
  computer's machine identifier; the identifier itself is not sent). Renewal sends the
  SDK Key only.
- Care&Co stores, for each SDK Key, its Target and the times it was activated, renewed
  and released, to administer seats and Grants.
- The device stores the signed SDK Key and the latest time the SDK has seen, so the
  license can be checked offline and a clock set back can be noticed; a clock set back
  by more than an hour leads to Basic Mode until it is corrected.
- A communication failure is not treated as an expiry, a release or a revocation.
- An SDK Key does not prove that a device is genuine, where code came from, or that an
  agreement is being complied with.

10. No SDK usage tracking

The SDK does not collect, retain or report activity records for the purpose of letting
Care&Co track how the SDK is used. It sends no measurement data, and does not report
whether or when the SDK was used, how many measurements or API calls were made, or use
after a Grant ended. Activation, renewal and release records (section 9) are records of
the SDK Key and its Target, not of SDK use; renewal does not show whether the SDK was
used or whether an agreement was complied with, and use without renewal never reaches
Care&Co.

This license does not restrict an application from storing measurement data and
reports for its own service.

